- Soulbits Cloud Config Convenience Features + Character Card Import (Complete, 2026-07-30):
  - Feature 1 — Cloud-aware endpoint prefill: `ModuleConfigEditScreen.handleProviderSwitch` prefills `base_url` with beta-aware `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` when switching to soulbitscloud while cloud-connected (`useSyncConnection().connectionStatus.mode === 'cloud'` && `isConnected`). Overrides the prod default in `PROVIDER_DEFAULTS.soulbitscloud.base_url` (the bug). Edit-mode untouched (stored value wins via `{...defaults, ...pConfig}`).
  - Feature 2 — Module-filtered model dropdown: new `src/components/config/SoulbitsModelSelect.tsx` renders for soulbitscloud `model` field (wired in `renderInlineProviderFields`). Loads models via new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts` (credential-less `createClient({inferenceURL})` → `client.models.listModelsOrThrow(query)` against public `GET /v1/models`; 5-min TTL cache + single-flight + never-throws → static fallback). Module-type→filter map in new `src/constants/soulbitsModels.ts`. Free-text "Custom…" override; saved-but-uncataloged model always shown. i18n in `moduleConfig.json`.
  - Shared infra (Phase 1-1): `FormField` `select` case renders new `src/components/config/SelectPicker.tsx` (themed Portal+Modal dropdown) instead of a disabled TextInput — fixes reasoning_effort/aspect_ratio select fields.
  - Feature 3 — Character card import: ported harmony-link-private `utils/charactercard/` (types.go/png_parser.go/mapper.go) to new pure-TS package `src/utils/charactercard/` (`types.ts`/`jsonParser.ts`/`pngParser.ts`/`mapper.ts`/`index.ts`). Parser: Tavern Card V1/V2/V3 from raw JSON or PNG-embedded tEXt/iTXt `chara`/`ccv3` chunks (base64-decoded; mirrors Go, no zlib/iTXt-compression). Mapper: → CharacterProfile + CharacterImage via `generateId()` (UUID v7), faithful field map + "CHARACTER LORE:"/"EXAMPLE DIALOGUES:" formatting. Import service `src/services/CharacterCardImportService.ts` (RNFS read → detect PNG/JSON → parse → map → persist via createCharacterProfile/createCharacterImage; typed errors: no_file/read_failed/unsupported_type/parse_failed/name_required). CharactersScreen header "Import Card" action (`@react-native-documents/picker` pick) + i18n in `characters.json`. Added `base64ToUint8Array` to `src/database/base64.ts`.
  - Tests: 6 new unit suites (jsonParser/pngParser/mapper/soulbitsModels/soulbitsModelsCatalog/base64) = 48 tests; full unit suite green (269 tests, 23 suites). tsc clean. GitNexus impact: all touched symbols LOW risk (callers local to edited files); detect_changes scope = 6 changed files, 5 affected processes (all the screens' own render/data flows). Manual/on-device verification deferred to user (build not run per workspace rules).
- Google OAuth Environment Secret Wiring (Complete, 2026-07-31): No hardcoded OAuth client IDs in tracked files. `scripts/oauth-secrets.cjs` (node, no deps) reads gitignored `client_secret_*.json` per env → writes `.env` (APP_ENV/IS_BETA/GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID/APPLE_SERVICES_ID) + `android/gradle-secrets.<env>.properties`. npm scripts: `oauth:dev`, `oauth:prod`; `android`/`ios`/`start` auto-load (start/E2E use `--if-missing-ok`). Android `build.gradle` flavor resolution: -P flag → gradle-secrets.<flavor>.properties → '' (removed hardcoded ID from gradle.properties). Runtime: `cloud.ts` `APP_ENVIRONMENT` export (env dev|prod + label); `react-native-config.d.ts` `APP_ENV`; `googleSignIn.ts` missing-ID warning. CI: build-release.yml iOS .env gen now includes APP_ENV; Android already passes vars.* via -P (priority). `.env` git-untracked; `client_secret_*.json`, `/secrets/`, `android/gradle-secrets.*.properties` all gitignored. Docs: `docs/OAUTH-SECRETS.md` (new) + INSTALLATION.md updated. Loader verified: resolves the provided dev client_secret JSON → writes .env + gradle-secrets.dev.properties (client ID intentionally not repeated here). Build/test deferred to user (per workspace rules).

- Engine & App Update Surfacing (Plan 7-10, Complete 2026-10-13): Release manifests (engine/latest.json + app/latest.json, static JSON on the existing CloudFront download hosts) + CI engine provisioning. Engine build.yml: new publish-release job publishes engine/<v>/{arm64,x86_64}/libengine.so + SoulbitsEngine.xcframework.zip + SoulbitsEngine.aar + NOTES.md and writes engine/<v>/manifest.json + engine/latest.json (contractVersion read from docs/api/management/openapi.yaml), then ws s3 ls verifies; both AWS jobs standardized to eu-central-1; Windows pwsh publish line got a first-run eyeball note. App build-release.yml: engine_version input + repo-var fallback, -PENGINE_SIDECAR_VERSION/BASE_URL/STRICT=true passthrough, APK libengine.so assertion, iOS xcframework fetch+unzip before pod install, app/latest.json writer in tag-only create-release. Gradle: retired the fictional ENGINE_SIDECAR_VERSION=0.1.0 default (CI-required explicitness) and added ENGINE_SIDECAR_STRICT (missing sidecar -> build FAILURE). Runtime: new utils/semver (semver-with-prerelease; v0.3.0-dev < 0.3.0); EngineApiClient.engineAppVersion() + EngineService contract canary (contract: ok|too_old|unknown) via an injected probe (engineVersionProbe.ts avoids the EngineApiClient<->EngineService cycle); EngineContractGate blocking card; UpdateAvailableService (both manifests, 6h AsyncStorage cache, cache-bust ?t=, env/flavor-aware, per-version dismissal) + UpdateBanner; About rows in HelpSupportSettingsScreen (app/engine/contract); DesktopSync rejected-state desktop-engine deep-link; optional Android APK self-update behind config/appChannel (sideload only; REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES + ApkInstallModule/ApkInstallPackage + apkSelfUpdate.ts). Work item 0 (prereq): BackupModule.pickFolder RN-0.86 fix (reactContext.currentActivity + reactContext.startActivityForResult). Gates: tsc 0; jest 131 suites/1102 tests; android gradlew assembleDevDebug BUILD SUCCESSFUL (first agent-verified Android build on this host). No management-contract changes. New i18n namespace updates (en). OWNER gates unchecked: first release run, manifest-shape sign-off, Play-vs-sideload channel decision, device drills.
- Release - Engine v0.4.6-dev + App v0.4.8-dev SHIPPED (2026-10-19): management contract 1.6.0 -> 1.7.0. The four stateless TTS voice routes the config editor calls (POST /api/module-configs/tts/embed-speaker, POST /api/module-configs/tts/test-speech, POST /api/providers/elevenlabs/voices/clone, POST /api/providers/elevenlabs/voices/design) were served by the engine router but absent from the spec/canonical fixtures. Engine (0b302f1): openapi paths + info.version 1.7.0, fixtures contractVersion 1.7.0 + manifest 49 -> 53 (+speakerEmbedding/ttsSpeechTest/elevenLabsVoiceClone/elevenLabsVoiceDesign), Management-API-Versioning.md, CHANGELOG, AppVersion -> v0.4.6-dev. App (e09cddc): ENGINE_CONTRACT_VERSION 1.7.0, four manifest entries ordered BEFORE /api/module-configs/:module/:id (loopback mock first-match), vendored typed fixtures, conformance + smoke drivers, docs/engine-contract-gates.md, versionName/MARKETING_VERSION 0.4.8. Engine android_only dispatch 39338563367 (both ABIs 200; 57.8 MB / 61.7 MB; no tag, engine/latest.json untouched); ENGINE_SIDECAR_VERSION -> v0.4.6-dev. App dispatch 39338937553 (version=v0.4.8, engine_version=v0.4.6-dev, publish_latest=true, build_ios=false) success: dev+prod APK 200 (106.9 MB each, libengine.so asserted), app/dev/latest.json = v0.4.8-dev, app/prod/latest.json still 403. Gates: engine build/vet/test green; app tsc 0; 190 suites/1799 tests; drift CLI 53/53; check:engine-contract green. CI repaired (c390407): test.yml never parsed (secrets.* in a step-level if: -> 0-job "workflow file issue" on every push); PAT mapped to job env + lint continue-on-error to match build-release.yml (~252 pre-existing lint errors / 810 warnings); Tests run 39338963384 green. No tags, no republish.
- Image Loading Performance (Complete 2026-10-20): management contract 1.7.0 -> 1.8.0. Thumbnails + metadata-only character image list. Engine (6d48407 + 379bfca): list no longer selects/encodes image_data (data_url only with ?include_data=1), migration 000054 thumbnail_data/thumbnail_mime (original never rewritten), 256px EXIF-oriented alpha-safe preview on upload + lazy backfill, GET .../images/:id?variant=thumb (404 + fallback:original sentinel), ETag/immutable cache, thumbnail_state tri-state ready|pending|unavailable (pending = pre-existing rows trigger backfill; has_thumbnail kept as state==ready), openapi image paths documented, fixtures 1.8.0 (manifest 53). App (881375b + 0ebac53): shouldUseThumbnail on display paths, LRU 64 + in-flight dedupe + 30s negative cache, FIFO cap 3 concurrent thumb fetches (originals uncapped), chat list paints rows first then hydrates avatars in parallel (one profile lookup per row), gallery tiles by URL, full-size viewer renders original by URL with X-Loopback-Token (animation preserved; Fresco animated-gif/animated-webp 3.6.0 added; APNG animates on iOS only). Releases: engine v0.4.6-dev -> v0.4.7-dev android_only run 39380789441 (arm64 55.6 MB, x86_64 59.4 MB, both 200; engine/latest.json untouched); app 0.4.8 -> 0.4.9 run 39381616102 (engine_version=v0.4.7-dev, publish_latest=true, build_ios=false). Gates: engine build/vet/test green; app tsc 0, 191 suites/1821 tests; drift 1.8.0/53/53. No tags.
- Image & Screen Load Follow-up (Complete 2026-10-20): Engine v0.4.8-dev (19a7b8a + 9fbdf0e, run 39395734476) + App v0.4.10 (5d64b99 + a04c3ce + ccd8aa9, run 39399585417). Bumped thumbnails to 512px q88 (4x pixel area), migration 000055 resets 256px thumbnails and adds chat-list/unread covering indexes, background startup thumbnail backfill (primaries first), Accept: application/vnd.soulbits.image-base64+json negotiation on image byte route, memoized LoadAllEntities(tx). App preserves lastMessage/unreadCount/pinned/archived/replyMode from entityChatList and character_profile_name from listEntities (cutting ChatListScreen first-paint from 64 HTTP [21 serial] + 300ms sleep to 3 parallel HTTP requests), dedupes in-flight profile/image-metadata reads, bypasses 3-slot semaphore for ready thumbnails, renders CharactersScreen grid before thumbnails and streams avatars progressively. Raised Gradle JVM to 4g/1g metaspace.
- TTS Test Studio Player Rework (Complete 2026-10-20): App v0.4.11 (55e8f66 + 3ca5416), engine v0.4.8-dev unchanged / no management-contract change. TtsTestPanel became a real player: root cause was fire-and-forget AudioPlayer.playAudio (resolves at playback start, nothing listened for the end) so the button sat on "Stop" forever; now polls getProgress/getState every 250ms (ChatBubble parity), renders a seekable player row (play/pause bubble, seek slider, 0:03 / 0:12 mono label via new src/utils/formatDuration.ts) and auto-resets on completion - instant replay for unchanged text, fresh synthesis when edited. Screen-dim -> background-exit -> biometric-lock fix: new first-party KeepScreenOn helper (Android FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON Kotlin module in keepawake/ + KeepScreenOnPackage() in MainApplication.kt; iOS idleTimerDisabled ObjC module in ios/KeepAwake/; no new npm dependency) held only while audio plays, released on pause/finish/unmount. Sample download button writes to the cache dir with react-native-fs and opens the OS share sheet with react-native-share (cancelled sheet is not an error). Paralinguistic chips capped at 20 behind a [+ N more] chip opening the searchable alphabetical TtsTagPickerModal (100+ tag models). New moduleConfig i18n keys (en). Gates: tsc 0, 193 suites / 1848 tests, targeted TTS 32/32. No tag, no push, no CI dispatch (owner gates).
- Bugfix Follow-up (Complete 2026-10-20): App v0.4.12 (fix 027d0d4 + release c4e6fbf + docs f2837f6). Fixed the Soulbits Cloud token cold-start race (auth:changed fires ~180ms before the engine management API connects -> soulbitscloud api-key refresh + seeding ensure dropped with Engine-is-not-connected warn -> engine kept an EXPIRED PASETO -> TTS test 401 token expired): shared engineReadiness.ts deferral helper (e2eEngineOverride retried-on-readiness pattern), refreshAllAndSync parks one retry (latest PASETO wins), dead syncCurrentToken() safety net wired to engine readiness (expired cached tokens skipped), ensureSeededDefaults defers the full paseto-less flow through its own freshness guard. Fixed App logs constant scroll-to-top (AppLogScreen onContentSizeChange scrollToOffset(0) fired on virtualization re-measures during the user's scroll — removed; follow/pause gates data only, like EngineLogScreen). Gates: tsc 0, 194 suites / 1868 tests (+20), detect_changes medium/all-intended. Engine v0.4.8-dev unchanged.
- Bugfix Round 2 (Complete 2026-10-20): App v0.4.13 (fix 5950497 + release 017a980 + docs). Fixed volume-key spurious backgrounding (RN emits background on ANY Activity onPause; HyperOS volume HUD pauses-but-visible -> every playback followed ~2s later by teardown of entity sessions/bubble/lock; web-research-verified mechanism; fix = new dep react-native-applifecycle@1.0.0, Android ON_START/ON_STOP semantics, swapped EntitySessionService/ChatBubbleService/BiometricLockContext(all flow+inactive-grace logic preserved)/LockScreen/OutreachNotificationService; lock confirmed NOT leaking while disabled). Fixed TTS declared-mp3-but-WAV-bytes (new src/utils/audioFormat.ts magic-byte sniffing + RIFF-header WAV duration, AudioPlayer sniff-first duration, TtsTestPanel resolveSynthesizedAudio stores actual mime for badge/download/share/duration). Gates: tsc 0, 197 suites / 1904 tests (+36), detect_changes HIGH breadth-flag all-intended. Engine v0.4.8-dev unchanged.
- CI Build-Time Optimization Tiers 1+3 (Complete 2026-10-20): commit 64c5183. Research-backed (GitHub cache = off-machine persistence restored onto each cold runner; caching=true alone useless cross-run; .cxx never cacheable; ubuntu-latest private = 2 vCPU): setup-gradle@v4 cache-read-only:false (dispatch branch is not default), org.gradle.caching=true, engine-sidecar actions/cache keyed on ENGINE_VERSION, -PVERSION_NAME replaces sed -i (sed defeated config-cache reuse), -PMETRO_MAX_WORKERS=2 opt-in, npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund, S3 latest pointer via server-side CopyObject. No app behavior change (197/1904 identical). Deferred: ABI trim, org.gradle.parallel, iOS tier. Measure warm effect on run 2 (run 1 only warms).
- CI Build-Time Optimization Tiers 1+3 VALIDATED (2026-10-20): run 39440030092 all green. Warm measurements: dev leg 12m09s (baseline 16m13s, -4m04s/-25%), prod leg 9m57s (baseline 13m06s, -3m09s/-24%) — matches the research estimate (2.5-5 min/leg). Latest-pointer server-side copy worked natively with --copy-props metadata-directive (ci-releases-uploader has GetObject/HeadObject, lacks only GetObjectTagging — grant the tagging perms in tofu if the fallback should ever become unnecessary). Engine-sidecar cache saved on run 2 -> next run also skips the ~115 MB download; expect further small gains as Gradle build-cache entries accumulate. Commits: 64c5183 (tiers 1+3), 405399c (pointer hotfix), 3a30b1b (docs).
- ABI Trim + Parallel Gradle (Complete 2026-10-20): App v0.4.14 (f0d7a6d + ccd85cf + docs). Owner-approved deferred tiers: reactNativeArchitectures -> arm64-v8a,x86_64 (32-bit was always engine-less, ~35 MB lighter APK, RN docs up to ~75% native build time), org.gradle.parallel=true (accepted 8GB-runner OOM risk, designated first revert, jvmargs untouched). No other repo ABI references needed changing. Gates: tsc 0, 197/1904 identical, gradle property resolution proven, detect_changes LOW. v0.4.14 dev dispatch = OOM watch + fastest-leg measurement (warm gradle cache + first sidecar-cache hit + 2 ABIs + parallel).
- ABI Trim + Parallel Gradel VALIDATED (2026-10-20): run 39443364468 all green, v0.4.14-dev published. No OOM with org.gradle.parallel=true on the 8GB runners (risk retired). Engine-sidecar cache hit (1-2s restore). Build-step measurements (same-flavor, warm cache): DEV 610s -> 408s (-33%, the trim+parallel effect is real); PROD 495s -> 517s (flat — but same-work legs spread +/-100-200s between runners: run-2's dev-vs-prod spread was 610/495, run-3's is 408/517, so single-leg comparisons carry runner variance; caches were fully warm, zero errors, no regression signal). Average build step across legs: 552s -> 462s. APK 108.5 -> 94.4 MB (-14.1 MB; the ~35MB estimate counted uncompressed libs — APK libs are compressed). WATCH-POINT: if the next 2-3 release runs consistently show prod build steps ~500s while dev sits ~410s, re-A/B org.gradle.parallel per leg.
- Dispatch Environment Selector (Complete 2026-10-20): commit 529a8d2. New build_environments input (dev|prod|both, default dev) drives build-android AND build-ios matrices via fromJSON expression; tags always both. publish-manifest mirrors via BUILT_ENVIRONMENTS: dev manifest only when dev built; prod manifest stays tag-only (prod-only dispatch = versioned APK + explicit notice). Truth table + bash-simulated shell paths A-D all pass. Dev-only dispatch halves CI cost. No app change.
